-- An input the existing parser rejects and the discovery stage accepts as the
-- language says: the existing lexer reads every brace of an interpolated pipe
-- string as a hole, and the hole `{kept}` has no `${...}` in the source, so
-- finalization reports it rather than give it another hole's location.
-- `KNOWN_DIVERGENCES` in `scripts/compiler-new-parity` lists it with its reason
-- (`docs/issues/interpolation_nesting_in_the_existing_lexer.md`).
-- Do not run the formatter on this file: it re-reads the string through the same
-- lexer and rewrites it as the lexer misreads it.
func pipe_braces(h: Int) -> String:
	text =
		|{kept} ${h} {kept}
		|more {text}
	text
